## Summary

Adds a type-safe, comptime-based hook system that allows games to register callbacks for engine lifecycle events with zero runtime overhead.

**Features:**
- `EngineHook` enum with lifecycle events (`game_init`, `game_deinit`, `scene_load`, `scene_unload`, `entity_created`, `entity_destroyed`, `frame_start`, `frame_end`)
- `HookPayload` tagged union for type-safe event data
- `HookDispatcher` comptime generic for zero-overhead dispatch
- `GameWith(Hooks)` generic to enable hooks, `Game = GameWith(void)` for backwards compatibility
- Hooks compile to no-ops when disabled (zero runtime overhead)
- Plugin hook support via custom enum/payload definitions

**Design decisions:**
- Comptime registration for zero runtime overhead (matches existing registry patterns)
- Hooks are purely observational (no cancellation)
- Separate dispatchers per plugin for clean namespacing
- Hooks disabled by default, enabled via `GameWith(MyHooks)`

**New files:**
- `src/hooks.zig` - Main module with re-exports
- `src/hooks/types.zig` - Hook enum and payload types  
- `src/hooks/dispatcher.zig` - Comptime dispatcher implementation
- `docs/rfcs/001-hook-system.md` - RFC documentation
- `usage/example_hooks/` - Working example demonstrating hook system

**Usage:**
```zig
const engine = @import("labelle-engine");

// Define hook handlers - only the hooks you care about
const MyHooks = struct {
    pub fn game_init(_: engine.HookPayload) void {
        std.log.info("[hook] Game initialized", .{});
    }

    pub fn frame_start(payload: engine.HookPayload) void {
        const info = payload.frame_start;
        std.log.info("[hook] Frame {d} started", .{info.frame_number});
    }

    pub fn scene_load(payload: engine.HookPayload) void {
        const info = payload.scene_load;
        std.log.info("[hook] Scene loaded: {s}", .{info.name});
    }
};

// Create Game type with hooks enabled
const Game = engine.GameWith(MyHooks);

pub fn main() !void {
    var game = try Game.init(allocator, config);
    // ... game_init hook fires automatically
    try game.run();
    // ... frame_start/frame_end hooks fire each frame
}
```

